    "done_when": "A new docs/research/scripts/scan_local_session_carryover.py reads, for every run under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs whose recorded backend is the local lane (clive), only the launch records and the first assistant turn of its stream, never the whole stream, and classifies each dispatch as fresh, same-task resume or cross-task resume with the first-turn input tokens and the tokens inherited against the fresh median. It uses the same classes, window rule and fields as codex-resume-burn-after.json, so the two files compare. It writes docs/research/data/local-session-carryover.json with a before window and an after window split at that commit time, and a positive control: one before-window local run known to be a cross-task resume, read through the same parser and classified cross_task with nonzero inherited tokens. An absence claim for the after window holds only if that control passes. The data file is at most 300 KB (per-run rows only for resumes and for a sample of at most 50 fresh runs); the scan runs in place on this compute node in under 20 minutes, and its wall time is recorded in the data. A new tests/test_local_session_carryover.py asserts the file's classes reconcile with its counts, the control is cross_task with nonzero inherited tokens, and the after window's cross-task count is the figure the file states. The named negative control (classify every dispatch as fresh) reddens the control assertion. The gate is tests/test_local_session_carryover.py and tests/test_resume_burn_after_the_fix.py at head, recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; the log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed paths report no finding. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete, printed and listed in artifacts. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/a-review-dies-where-nobody-is-looking/local-session-carryover.html states both windows' counts and inherited-token totals beside the codex figures, with one figure under docs/figures/a-review-dies-where-nobody-is-looking/local-session-carryover/ comparing the classes before and after on both lanes: no gridlines, top and right spines removed, series labelled directly. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
